# kitting: bimanual human-demo dataset from h2r_collection, exported as
# LeRobot v2.1 and converted to v3.0 (scripts/convert_v21_to_v30_local.py).
#
# Modalities (verbatim from the dataset's meta/info.json: 141 episodes, 20613
# frames, 30 fps; 95/141/299 frames per episode min/median/max):
#   cameras: observation.images.{head, wrist_left, wrist_right}  (720x1280 video)
#   state:   observation.state  (14)   } identical names/layout, absolute values:
#   action:  action             (14)   }
#       0-2  left.wrist.x/y/z      3-5   left.wrist.roll/pitch/yaw
#       6-8  right.wrist.x/y/z     9-11  right.wrist.roll/pitch/yaw
#       12   left.gripper          13    right.gripper
#     i.e. BOTH wrists first, THEN both grippers -- not xyz/rpy/grip per arm.
#     So the Euler-angle dims are 3,4,5,9,10,11 and the grippers are 12,13.
#     Same layout as gear_left, so checkpoints of the two are interchangeable
#     as far as the wire format goes.
#   task:    "pick the black object and place it inside the box"  (1 task —
#            unlike gear_left, this one carries a language annotation)
#
# Inpaint cache size: 20613 frames x 3 cameras = 61839 frames to warm
# (~5-6 h across two GPUs at ~0.65 s/frame), 3x gear_left's.
#
# Data-quality note, measured on the v3 export: the RIGHT wrist track is
# noticeably jumpier than the left -- 446 frame-to-frame position jumps > 5 cm
# across 56 of the 141 episodes (left: 23 jumps across 16 episodes), with single
# frames moving up to 0.43 m. At 30 fps those are tracking glitches, not motion.
# They are left in deliberately (the dataset is read-only and untouched), but
# expect the right arm's relative-action stats to be wider than the left's.

# The dataset id and its local copy are machine-specific: the HF account and the
# dataset root come from the untracked configs/local.env (see LOCAL_SETUP.md),
# and this config only names itself. Anything already set in the environment
# wins, which is how scripts/chain.sh passes an explicit dataset through.
_local="${BASH_SOURCE[0]%/*}/local.env"
if [[ -f "$_local" ]]; then
    source "$_local"
else
    echo "WARNING: $_local not found; set DATASET/DATASET_ROOT yourself" >&2
fi
unset _local

DATASET=${DATASET:-${HF_OWNER:-local}/kitting}
# Only fill the root in if that copy actually exists; otherwise leave it empty
# and let lerobot resolve the dataset from the HF cache.
if [[ -z ${DATASET_ROOT+set} && -d "${DATASETS_ROOT:-}/kitting" ]]; then
    DATASET_ROOT=$DATASETS_ROOT/kitting
fi

# pi0 only: pi0_base has three fixed camera slots with openpi names; map ours onto
# them (baked into the checkpoint's preprocessor, reused at inference).
# GR00T needs no map: with embodiment_tag=new_embodiment it takes the dataset's
# camera keys as-is and records them in its modality_configs.
PI0_RENAME_MAP='{"observation.images.head": "observation.images.base_0_rgb", "observation.images.wrist_left": "observation.images.left_wrist_0_rgb", "observation.images.wrist_right": "observation.images.right_wrist_0_rgb"}'

# Inpainting methods applied on the fly at dataloader time (arm inpainting, ...).
# Uncomment to remove the demonstrator's arm/hand from every training frame
# (Grounding DINO -> SAM2 -> LaMa; see src/h2r_il/inpainting/). Dataset stays
# read-only. A method name, or a JSON spec for tuning, e.g.
#   INPAINTING='[{"name":"arm_inpaint","dilation":21,"prompt":"arm. hand."}]'
# INPAINTING=arm_inpaint
# INPAINTING_CACHE=  # defaults to outputs/inpaint_cache; override per machine

# Object-pose target for the auxiliary loss. All perception ran up front
# (h2r_il.object_pose_dataset track + store); training only looks the pose up by
# the global frame index each sample already carries, so the dataset stays
# read-only and there is no dataloader cost. The head-camera store below covers
# all 141 episodes at 0.48 cm median depth error against MoGe.
#   OBJECT_POSE_TARGET=position (default) emits xyz; pose6d adds a wxyz
#   quaternion. Prefer position: rotation comes from an arbitrary SAM3D body
#   frame and nothing in the pipeline validates it.
# Every sample also carries observation.object_pose_valid, and the loss masks on it
# (h2r_il.losses.object_pose) -- without that, frames with no pose would train the
# model towards a pose of all zeros.
#
# Setting OBJECT_POSE both attaches the target AND switches the policy type to the
# h2r variant that consumes it (h2r_groot here, h2r_pi0 for ft_pi0.sh, which needs
# its checkpoint re-staged first -- see scripts/stage_h2r_policy.py). The head is
# on the shared trunk, so the aux gradient shapes the representation.
#   OBJECT_POSE_WEIGHT=1.0   aux weight; the target is standardised first, so this
#                            is a preference, not a unit conversion
#   OBJECT_POSE_HEAD=0       attach the target but train stock groot (plumbing check)
#   OBJECT_POSE_DETACH=1     passive probe: measure whether the trunk already
#                            encodes object position, without shaping it
# OBJECT_POSE=outputs/object_pose/kitting/head/store
# OBJECT_POSE_TARGET=position
# OBJECT_POSE_WEIGHT=1.0

# ABSOLUTE actions (2026-08-05): the policy predicts `action` verbatim, the same
# 14-dim absolute pose the dataset records. This is the second arm of the action
# -space ablation -- kitting_v1_inpaint (relative) vs kitting_v1abs_inpaint
# (absolute), same data, same inpainting cache, same hyperparameters.
#
# Everything below is the relative-action setup, kept commented so switching back
# is a one-line change rather than a re-derivation. NOTE: ft_groot.sh tests
# RELATIVE_ACTIONS with `[[ -n ... ]]` -- presence, not truth -- so it must be
# *empty or absent* for absolute. `RELATIVE_ACTIONS=0` would still turn relative
# actions ON. RELATIVE_ANGLE_DIMS must go too: chain.sh's export_hooks exports
# H2R_RELATIVE_ANGLE_DIMS whenever it is non-empty, and it only has meaning for
# the relative conversion.
#
# Relative EEF actions: policy predicts (action - current state) for the 12 wrist
# dims; the grippers (12,13) stay absolute. RELATIVE_ANGLE_DIMS makes the
# conversion angle-aware -- here it is LEFT.wrist.yaw that crosses the +pi/-pi
# seam (6 crossings, in episodes 4, 6 and 139; gear_left's seam is on the right
# wrist instead). A plain subtraction turns each crossing into a ~2pi delta,
# ~400x the median step, which would dominate GR00T's min/max relative-action
# stats. All six Euler dims are listed so the fix does not depend on which
# wrist happens to wrap in a given recording.
# RELATIVE_ACTIONS=1
# RELATIVE_EXCLUDE_JOINTS='["gripper"]'
# RELATIVE_ANGLE_DIMS='[3,4,5,9,10,11]'
